# rule.always.question-the-need-behind-an-ask

> **an ask assumes a frame and serves a need. receipt first, then: restate it, name the need, test the frame by a read, answer the need and the words.**

cues: an ask names a state as fact → read it · a decision a read could carry → answer from the read, hand back the decision · a yes/no on a means → answer the end · two answers offered as the only two → look for the third · the same ask returns → the need was never met.
test: **what does the asker need, and what does the ask assume?**
blocker: an ask answered on its words while a read refutes the frame it assumes
nitpick: an ask answered with no need named · the why of an ask used to dodge it
